<title>ITALY: Italian bonds/futures closing report.</title>
<headline>Italian bonds/futures closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian bond futures surged in late trading after a flat start, breaking through resistance at 115.15, and closed sharply higher on hopes of a new Bank of Italy discount rate cut, traders said.</p>
<p>A firmer lira against the mark and good tone in bunds also underpinned sentiment, but traders said they were surprised by the strength of the rise.</p>
<p>Hopes of a fresh Bank of Italy discount rate cut were rekindled by market rumours in the afternoon after this morning's meeting between Prime Minister Romano Prodi and central bank governor Antonio Fazio.</p>
</text>
